t are never clean. If a tree falls across the path, it remains there. Everybody who takes the path has to climb over it. If a bridge collapses, it remains for months and years, until it is replaced. [Page 243] Training the islanders in orderly activity, punctuality, and cleanliness will take much time and effort.\'  We have assumed that tree or liana bridges were present in some form in the pre-colonial period as well. This is open to re-consideration.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 970, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 897})
